<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n52555" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κᾰλάσῑρις</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[λᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιος</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a long Egyptian garment</i>, with tassels or fringe
			at bottom, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.81
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				30
			</span></i>; also, <i>a Persian garment</i> of like kind,
				<i><span class="en">
				Democr.Eph.
				1
			</span></i>; used in the Mysteries of Andania, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(1).1390.17
			</span></i> (in form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλάσηρις</span></b> ):—title of a Comedy of Alexis. Cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρυφοκαλάσῑρις</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as pr. n., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καλασίριες, οἱ</span>, a branch
			of the military caste in Egypt, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.164
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
